config OTA_RELEASE_REPO
    string "GitHub repository to check for firmware releases"
    default "a9650615/esp32-rlcd-standalone"
    help
        "owner/name" of the repository whose latest release is offered as a
        firmware update on the settings page. Change this if you forked the
        project, or the device will offer you someone else's builds.

        The check is read-only and never installs on its own: it reports what
        it found and leaves the decision on the settings page.

        Unauthenticated GitHub API requests are rate-limited per source
        address (60/hour at the time of writing), which is ample for a check
        driven by a button press.

config OTA_RELEASE_ASSET_SUFFIX
    string "Filename suffix identifying the firmware asset in a release"
    default ".bin"
    help
        A release can carry several attachments. The first asset whose name
        ends with this suffix is treated as the firmware image.

        Note that a wrong choice here is not dangerous: whatever is downloaded
        still has to pass the image header check before a single byte of the
        OTA slot is erased.
